From a4e95798251a8e1d6d5c3a0036150e72c20adc97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:41:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] 02-rights candidate: PS2 records for every Grant
 instruction

Every Grant instruction now logs one chained PS2 record: GRANT_ISSUED,
SWAP_RESERVED, SWAP_EXECUTED, SWAP_RELEASED, GRANT_REVOKED and
GRANT_CLOSED. The kind codes 200-205 are provisional and not
allocated: they are far from 104-112, which workstreams 8 and 10
propose, and the integrator confirms or moves them. The kinds join the
shared v2 log table, because CQ1 decodes records only through it, with
entity tables (chains_of) that name each holding a record moved and no
optional link. Payload encoders live in frontier_abi::v2::rights::record
for the program and the verifier alike. The record-width bounds
(events::MAX_KIND_V2, cqlog::MAX_KIND) rise to 205.

Host tests capture sol_log_data through a cfg(test) syscall stub,
decode every record with the ABI decoder, check that its amounts are
what the holdings moved, and check that each link equals the chain
header of the account chains_of names. No key is generated or used.

